  "reason": "The assertions are not equivalent because the relationship definitions describe fundamentally different structural realities. The qualified_original uses 'connect_via' with the definition 'SOURCE establishes structural linkage to TARGET', which accurately reflects that neurons link to synapses (the interface points). In contrast, the qualified_proposal uses 'form' with the definition 'indicates that the source constructs or constitutes the target'. This implies that neurons physically build or make up the synapse itself. Since a neuron does not constitute a synapse (it connects *to* one), the proposal introduces a false claim of structural composition/constitution that is absent in the original assertion."
